SteamARM: Fill, Center and Move & Resize in XQuartz's Window menu

macOS 15's tiling commands for X windows, which are not NSWindows: Fill
(Globe-Control-F), Center (Globe-Control-C) and a "Mover y redimensionar"
(Move & Resize) submenu with the halves, the quarters and Return to
Previous Size (Globe-Control-R), after Zoom and before the list of windows.
They go to the window manager as an AppleWMControllerNotify of kind 32
with the action in its argument (quartz-wm-tiling.patch); the wire format
already carries any kind and argument. Built in code, Spanish or English
from the user's first language: the menus live in compiled nibs. No arrow
shortcuts: arrow keys always carry the Function flag, and Control-arrow
belongs to terminals. XQUARTZ_NO_TILING_MENU=1 leaves the menu as it was.
